Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:06.720
Is "Skinamarink" the "scariest film ever made"?&nbsp;
Or a nonsensical nightmare? Why not both?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.180
Every year, a new horror movie comes along&nbsp;
that's billed as an all-timer. 2022 saw the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.860
release of "Terrifier 2," an independent&nbsp;
slasher that became an unlikely mainstream&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.620
success story after it made fans physically sick&nbsp;
at screenings. This year, though, "Skinamarink"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.660
is the hot new horror flick on the block that&nbsp;
people are already hailing as a future classic.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.720
"Skinamarink" has, in fact, been described as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:35.280
"the scariest film ever made" by some&nbsp;
shaken reviewers. That's high praise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.720
and it remains to be seen if it will stand the&nbsp;
test of time, but there's no denying that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:44.760
hype surrounding Kyle Edward Ball's debut&nbsp;
feature is exciting and morbidly alluring.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.380
"Skinamarink" is the type of horror movie&nbsp;
that taps into the primal essence of fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.680
according to the TwitterVerse.&nbsp;
